 "conclusions": [
  "13 of the 15 failing treatment cells genuinely exhausted 6000 expansions; the label was right for them.",
  "sc25 terminated after 24 expansions having discovered 1 distinct state, at BOTH 6000 and 30000. g50t terminated after 4100 expansions / 843 states, also identically at both budgets. For these two the 5x-budget probe was VACUOUS -- no budget increase could have changed the outcome -- so exp6093's 'capability wall, not a budget wall' reading is right for 9 of the 11 still-failing games and WRONG IN KIND for sc25 and g50t, whose failure is a frontier collapse under the generic state abstraction.",
  "cn04 and dc22 were re-probed at 30000 and genuinely exhausted it (30000 expansions, 6173 and 1088 distinct states), anchoring the 9-game exhaustion reading.",
  "On the 10 games the generic explorer DOES solve, it reaches the same level for 95-3544 expansions against the adaptered arm's 3-3970 -- a median ~145x more search for the same move count. Per-game knowledge buys roughly two orders of magnitude of search efficiency even where it is not necessary for success.",
  "None of this moves exp6093's headline: 24/25 -> 10/25, the sign test (0 better / 11 ties / 14 worse, p=0.000122) and 14/25 at 5x budget are all unaffected. A frontier collapse is still a failure to bank L1."
 ],
